    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d869">

                <pb facs="0902" n="890" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg890"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.51/5–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-05T18:00:00+03:06">May 5, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>193. ReDepts No. 130, May 3, 6 p.m. While 2 months ago King Abdul Aziz would have
                    been quite receptive to proposals confined to subject of my approaching visit I
                    expect him to demand information on matters of greater urgency to him now (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) subsidy program for 1945 (Department’s No. 125,
                    April 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">27</hi>], 6 p.m.) and (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>) expectations of long range financial aid (Department’s No. 283,
                    December 24, 2 p.m.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d869-f1"/>)</p>
                <p>If possible can Department authorize me to make any statement on either subject
                    during this visit? Locust plague, non-delivery of cereals and spare parts, lack
                    of any indication whether his budget will be balanced disturb him profoundly
                    Minister of Finance<anchor n="96" xml:id="d869-f2"/> informs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
